     No, cracking knuckles does not cause arthritis. The popping sound results from gas bubbles collapsing in synovial fluid, not bone grinding. A 50-year self-experiment by Dr. Donald Unger (cracking only one hand) found no difference in arthritis between hands. A 2011 study of 215 adults aged 50–89 found no association between habitual knuckle cracking and hand osteoarthritis. Rarely, forceful cracking may cause ligamen
     sources: https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/9811062/, https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21300873/, https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28196461/
